# V-TAPP Dashboard — environment
#
# Copy to .env.local for development. On AWS Amplify these go under
# App settings → Environment variables, and amplify.yml carries them
# into the SSR runtime.
#
# .env.local is gitignored. Never commit real values: the service role
# key bypasses every row-level policy in the database.

# ── Supabase ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Project settings → API. The anon key is safe in the browser; the
# service role key is not and must stay server-side.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR-PROJECT.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# ── Upstream V-TAPP feed ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Where registrations are synced from.
VTAPP_API_URL=
VTAPP_API_KEY=

# ── This app ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The public origin, with no trailing slash. Two jobs:
#
#   1. The absolute base for QR links inside emails.
#   2. The fallback when a CDN forwards a request without rewriting the
#      Host header. CloudFront does exactly that: the origin sees
#      "localhost:3000", and without this every redirect -- including
#      the Google sign-in callback -- sends people to their own
#      machine. See lib/origin.ts.
#
# Get this wrong and sign-in breaks, not just the email links.
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=https://vtapp.co.in

# Where "Register or buy merchandise" sends a student with nothing on
# their account.
NEXT_PUBLIC_EVENTS_PORTAL_URL=https://events.vitap.ac.in

# ── Mail ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ZeptoMail (Zoho), transactional relay on the verified domain
# vtapp.co.in. Gmail was the first host here and is what the fallbacks
# and the 450 cap below still assume; it caps a trial account at ~500
# recipients a day, which is five days to send 1,800 passes.
#
# SMTP_USER is the literal string "emailapikey" -- not an address.
# SMTP_PASSWORD is the send-mail token from the ZeptoMail console.
#
# MAIL_FROM is therefore NOT optional here. It falls back to SMTP_USER,
# and "emailapikey" in a From header is rejected by every message.
# It must also be on a domain verified in ZeptoMail; the app refuses
# to start a batch otherwise and says which setting is at fault.
#
# Until SMTP_USER and SMTP_PASSWORD are both set, nothing sends: every
# send returns "skipped" and the app behaves exactly as it does now.
SMTP_HOST=smtp.zeptomail.in
SMTP_PORT=587
SMTP_USER=emailapikey
SMTP_PASSWORD=
MAIL_FROM=noreply@vtapp.co.in
MAIL_FROM_NAME=V-TAPP 2026

# Messages in flight at once. Defaults to 1 when SMTP_HOST looks like
# Gmail (it throttles parallel connections from one account) and 5
# otherwise, which is most of the speed gained by moving off Gmail.
# Raise cautiously: past this the limit is the relay's, not ours.
# MAIL_CONCURRENCY=5

# SMTP_USERNAME, SMTP_FROM_EMAIL and SMTP_FROM_NAME are accepted as
# aliases for the three above, since that is what most SMTP tooling
# calls them. The names above win if both are set.

# Where sync failures are reported. Your own address, not the sending
# mailbox — an alert nobody reads is not an alert.
ALERT_EMAIL=

# How many messages may go out in a rolling 24 hours.
#
#   ZeptoMail                credits    -> 5000 (free credit = 10,000)
#   Google Workspace, paid   ~2000/day  -> 1800
#   Google Workspace, TRIAL   ~500/day  ->  450 (the default)
#
# Defaults to 450 whatever the host, deliberately: the cost of a
# too-low default is pressing the button again, and the cost of a
# too-high one on Gmail is a locked account and a day of silence
# mid-fest. On ZeptoMail there is no daily cliff at all -- credits are
# spent, not refused -- so this becomes a spend limit rather than a
# safety limit. Raise it there.
#
# On Gmail, limits are NOT raised during a trial, and converting to
# paid is not enough on its own: Google raises them only after the
# domain has cumulatively paid $100 USD, and then up to 75 days later.
# See docs/email-setup.md.
MAIL_DAILY_CAP=5000
